            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-gray-700">Direct Google + CSLB</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-green-600">No</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-red-500">DIY</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-yellow-600">Maybe</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-center text-green-600">Yes</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Section -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary text-center mb-10">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      {[
        { q: "Why doesn't Thumbtack work well for tree service emergencies?", a: "Thumbtack is designed for non-urgent project bidding. When you submit a tree service request, contractors submit bids over the following hours — which is fine for a kitchen remodel but completely wrong when you have a tree on your roof after a Santa Ana windstorm. Emergency tree situations require calling a company directly with 24/7 availability, not waiting for a bid competition to play out." },
